  "asked": "# Build: settings-sections-everywhere ## Brett said (verbatim) \"All groups of settings in every settings interface as of now, everything, it's gotta be in sections. Everything's gonna be arranged in sections that are similar: certain types of settings in a section that's collapsible. Every settings interface that is in existence thus far is gonna be like that. You're gonna go through and refactor them, put everything in categories. And they're all collapsible sections.\" 1. Inventory every settings interface in console, AmberX, Molly, axHub web, Expenses and every plugin. Report the list and the categories chosen for each. 2. Framework: the settings-interface asset (settings-ui@1) gets sections: title, icon, order, collapsed-by-default, fold state remembered per device; expand/collapse all. Reuse FoldSections from notes-views. 3. Refactor every existing settings interface into categorized collapsible sections (similar settings grouped). No setting removed or renamed. 4. CI check: a settings interface with ungrouped settings fails. 5. Tests, README, report, screenshots to UI Review, PR to the merge queue. Do NOT land directly. Coordinate with claude-settings-tabs-veto (queued): its tabs sit above these sections; don't rebuild its work. One session, lean chain. Stay out of Gizmo, UI registry, badges/notifications code (other builds). Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
